# Choosing a schema

## Default — start with a **star**

- Flat, denormalized dims: **fastest, simplest, BI-friendly**
- Make it the default; deviate only with a reason

## Snowflake — by exception, per dimension

- A **huge** dim with a repetitive sub-tree (real storage saving)
- A **shared** sub-dim → an **outrigger** (Jabra `DIM_GEOGRAPHY`)
- A **tool / governance** rule mandating normalized data
- Snowflake the *one* dim that needs it — a scalpel, not the default

## Galaxy — grow into it

- Model one process as a star · add the next **reusing conformed dims**
- Plan with the **bus matrix**

## Modern tilt

- Columnar MPP → cheaper joins & storage → **even more star** (module 10)
